# Design review: window manager — 30 Oct 2026

Bob walked through the compositor.

- Windows move with transforms during interaction; layout properties are written once at the end.
- Pointer capture is used on title bars, which fixed the problem where fast drags lost the window.
- Focus and z-order are one ordered list; clicking moves the window to the end.
- The dock uses a single rAF loop for magnification instead of one per icon.

Review comments:
- Dan: the compositor should not import any app code (boundary rule) — agreed.
- Esha: add a frame-time assertion to the e2e drag test (p95 ≤ 16.7 ms).
- Alice: Exposé thumbnails should be static snapshots, not live DOM clones, to save memory.

Outcome: approved with the two follow-ups.
